PlannedWorkout.description:
A workout a provider's calendar plans for the athlete — prescribed by a
coach or a plan on `TrainingPeaks`, a Garmin calendar, Intervals.icu —
read back as the provider states it.

Every planned figure is optional because providers state them
independently: a coach may write a title and a duration and nothing
else. The steps use the periodization kernel's [`WorkoutStep`], with each
step's target in the [`RelativeIntensity`](crate::periodization::RelativeIntensity)
grammar, so a planned session and a Dravr-authored one read the same way.

# Examples

```rust
use chrono::NaiveDate;
use dravr_cageux::models::{PlannedWorkoutBuilder, SportType};

# fn main() -> Result<(), &'static str> {
let date = NaiveDate::from_ymd_opt(2026, 9, 24).ok_or("not a calendar date")?;
let workout = PlannedWorkoutBuilder::new(
    "trainingpeaks",
    "2941803311",
    date,
    SportType::Ride,
    "Sweet spot 3x12",
)
.planned_duration_seconds(4500)
.planned_training_stress_score(78.0)
.build();

assert_eq!(workout.title(), "Sweet spot 3x12");
assert_eq!(workout.planned_duration_seconds(), Some(4500));
# Ok(())
# }
```

sex.description:
Physiological sex, as the athlete stated it or a provider reported it;
absent when neither did. It selects the published equations that take
one.

profile.description:
The profile as it now stands, re-read from storage after a write;
absent when the athlete has none and nothing was imported. Its
`threshold_provenance` names every value a provider supplied.

